PS+=['Sandy: Dave is not going to the movies with us this weekend. It’s the second time this month. It’s strange.\nGreg: Well, maybe it’s because he is seeing someone. In fact, I saw him with a beautiful woman at a tea house the other day.\nSandy: What’s the tea, Greg?\nGreg: Too bad! They had coffee, not tea.\nSandy: No, Greg. I mean I want to know more about Dave and the woman!\nGreg: Oh, I see. Well, they were at a nice tea house on York Street. I was reading when I saw them.\nSandy: And then?\nGreg: Dave had a sandwich, and the woman ordered a strawberry pie. And...\nSandy: I am not interested in the food. Get to the point!\nGreg: OK. OK. It looked like they had a great time together. They talked about many things like their hobbies, favorite songs, and so on. By the way, Dave called the woman Liz.\nSandy: Aww, that’s sweet. Are they going to meet up again?\nGreg: I think so. They talked about visiting the Modern Art Museum or something.\nSandy: Forget about the movie. Let’s go follow Dave this weekend! I want to see the woman in person! What do you say?\nGreg: Of course not. We know nothing about this woman because Dave does not want us to know about her. As his best friends, we should just wait until he’s ready to share.\nSandy: All right. Let’s keep to our first plan. See you then.\n（likely 可能；dialogue 對話）']
