PS+=['【Andrew】Why did Eric shout at me today?\nI really don’t understand. I took those photos just to make a great video for him, and I never meant to hurt or laugh at him. During the 8 months, he worked very hard to lose weight for the dance show. Wasn’t it a great idea to take a picture every week to record his changes?\n\n【Nancy】RE: Why did Eric shout at me today?\nI almost cried when I was watching the video. To be honest, I already forgot about Eric’s size before watching it. He’s now a lot thinner than before! Maybe Eric was not angry with you. He just felt embarrassed when you showed the video to everyone. Believe me, he will thank you for making the video in the future.\n\n【Joshua】RE: Why did Eric shout at me today?\nI like the video, too. It was hard to notice Eric’s changes because we saw him every day. However, the 35 photos in the video showed us his hard work perfectly. In fact, I think Eric liked it, too. He was angry just because you took those photos without telling him first. No one likes that.\n\n【Phoebe】RE: Why did Eric shout at me today?\nTo give Eric a surprise doesn’t sound like a good reason to me. Eric tried so hard to lose weight, and he doesn’t want anyone to remember his past self. It might be great to make the video for Eric as a gift, but it was a big mistake to play it in front of the class without letting him know first. You’d better say sorry to Eric as soon as possible.\n（weight 重量；record 記錄；embarrassed 尷尬的；perfectly 完美地）']
