PS+=['Training Date: 2023/06/19\nWhat Should You Do When You See a Bear?\nNever Attack, Run, Shout, or Look at Its Eyes!!\n\n▸ If the bear is far away:\nQuietly leave that area right away. Do NOT run or make loud noises.\n▸ If the bear starts getting close to you:\nSlowly and quietly move and leave. Do NOT turn your back on the bear.\n▸ If the bear stands on its hind legs:\nIt might not be trying to attack you. It may just be curious. Bears sometimes stand to look farther. Still, you should back away slowly.\n▸ If the bear charges at you:\nIn most cases, the bear does this to test you. This charge is usually short. It’ll run up to you and then suddenly stop. Then it turns back.\nYou can ring your bear bell to make the bear go away.\nOR\nYou can wave things in your hand or raise your hands to make yourself look larger.\n（hind 後方的；curious 好奇的；charge (at) 猛衝（向）；suddenly 突然）']
