PS+=['Here are three living things—three-toed sloths, sloth moths, and trichophilus. They look far different from one another. However, there is a strong tie among them. It may be much more interesting than you think!\n【Three-Toed Sloth】Meet the three-toed sloth, probably the slowest animal in the world. These sloths don’t get enough energy from their food, so they move very little to save energy. However, when nature calls, they s-l-o-w-l-y climb down the trees. Although it is dangerous for them to go down to the ground and poop, they still do it once a week. Why don’t they just defecate in the trees?\n【Sloth Moth】The sloths have some little friends—sloth moths! These moths live in the hair of the sloths because it’s like a comfortable hotel for them. They need the sloths to defecate on the ground so that they can lay eggs in their poop. The baby insects grow up in the poop. Then, they move back to live in the hair of the sloths when the sloths climb down the trees. After the sloth moths die, their bodies become trichophilus’ food.\n【Trichophilus】That’s right. Trichophilus is the third member in this cool circle. It is very special, and people can’t find it anywhere else but on the sloths. Trichophilus makes some parts of the sloths’ bodies look green and helps them hide in the trees. What’s more, the sloths get to eat some trichophilus when they are cleaning their hair. Eating this plant is also a great help to the sloths’ health.\n（among 在……之間；defecate 排便；energy 能量；poop 排便；糞便；lay 下蛋）']
