PS+=['Ideas from Around — Richard Smith\n【Our City, Our Home】\nWhen people say our city is far from being good or convenient enough, I totally agree. However, when they start to get angry at the government and keep asking for more, well, I can’t agree with that. In fact, the government is doing much more than many people think.\nTake the benches outside the public library for example. They were there for people to sit on and read a book. Together with the trees, they used to make the library look like a wonderful place. However, some people slept on them for hours, and others enjoyed their food on the benches but didn’t clean them up. In the end, the government had no choice but to remove all the benches to keep the area clean.\nThe benches show us only a very small part of the problem. To enjoy things in public places, we all should learn to use them in the right way. If some people only think about themselves, they may cause trouble for others. Getting angry with them is surely not helpful. To me, teaching them a lesson by giving them a fine is not enough, either.\nWe must go further to deal with the problem by starting with young kids in school. It is more important than getting good grades. If we only teach them subjects like English and math, how can we expect them to grow into great citizens in the future? We need lessons to teach our children to take care of our city. This way, we can reach out to the next generation and truly help the city get better. After all, a city can only be good when it has good citizens.\n（government 政府；remove 移除；cause 造成；citizen 公民；generation 世代）']
D+=[
(37,'What does Richard Smith think of the city government?',['It never spends people’s money wisely.','It actually does a lot to make the city better.','It does many things, but most of them are not helpful at all.','It should learn to listen to its people carefully.'],[],len(PS)-1),
(38,'Why did Richard Smith talk about the benches outside the public library?',['He wanted to give an example of people’s wrong ways of using the things in a public place.','He brought that up to tell people to remember the history of the city.','He wanted everyone to take action to get those benches back.','He talked about that because he was really mad at the government.'],[],len(PS)-1),
(39,'According to Richard Smith, why is it important to teach kids about taking care of the city?（according to 根據）',['It helps them learn English and math better.','It makes them use public places more often.','It helps them become better citizens in the future.','It gives them the power to rule other people.'],[],len(PS)-1),
]
PS+=['【Dengue Fever Spraying Notice】\nAfter the rainy season, the number of dengue fever cases keeps rising. In order to stop it, there will be wide spraying in this area at 10:00 a.m. on July 28. The spraying covers not only the outdoor areas but also the inside space of your house, including your living room, kitchen, bathrooms, and bedrooms. The spraying will last for about 30 minutes.\n\nBefore the Spraying:\n❶ Please check inside and around your house carefully for any items with water in them and clean them up.\n❷ Please put all food, plates, bowls, and so on into drawers or boxes.\n❸ Feel free to cover items like sofas and beds. However, your covering should not stop the spraying from going into every corner of the space.\n❹ Close all your windows and doors.\n❺ Pets must leave. If you have fish, cover your fishbowl and turn off the air pump.\n❻ Please hand your key to a neighbor if you aren’t home. We will enter your house with the help of the police when no one is home.\n\nAfter the Spraying:\n❶ Wait for 1 hour after the spraying. Once you enter your house, open the windows and doors to let fresh air in first, and then wait outside for another 30 minutes.\n❷ Please be careful as the floor might be a little wet.\n❸ The repellent will not hurt your health, but it’s a good idea to wash your hands after you touch the items with the repellent on them.\n\nIf you have any questions, please call the Health Department at 12-334-556. Thank you for your help and understanding. Let’s save our town from dengue fever together!\nHealth Department, Brooklyn\n（dengue fever 登革熱；spraying 噴藥；including 包括；pump 幫浦；repellent 驅蟲劑）']
