PS+=['There are many stories in the history of music. To some people, Jean-Baptiste Lully’s death is probably the saddest and most surprising one.\nLully was a gifted musician from Italy. He was born in 1632 and was famous for making beautiful music. He showed his interest in music when he was very young. After he moved to France, he learned more and was able to bring his own music to a new level. People loved listening to his music, and he even became King Louis XIV’s favorite.\nLully was good at writing music. Also, he was proud to hold a conducting staff and lead a group of musicians. ＿42＿ It was long, heavy, and not easy to use. However, no one saw that as a problem until January 1687.\nIn 1687, something sad happened. When Lully was conducting his own music Te Deum, he struck his foot with the conducting staff by mistake. Although doctors tried their best to help him, Lully’s foot got terribly infected in a short time. ＿43＿\nLully’s death marked a turning point in the history of conducting. Now, we have lighter and better tools for conducting. And of course, Lully’s music lives on and keeps bringing joy to people even today.\n（musician 音樂家；conducting staff 指揮棒；conduct 指揮；strike 擊中（過去式 struck）；infected 感染的）']
D+=[
(42,'第 42 格應填入：',['In fact, a lot of musicians in France wanted Lully to teach and to lead them.','The conducting staff of Lully’s time was very different from today’s conducting tool.','To Lully, leading a group of musicians was much easier than writing music.','But Lully never thought about killing anyone with the conducting staff.'],[],len(PS)-1),
(43,'第 43 格應填入：',['He even wrote several songs about his days in the hospital.','After that, Lully could only use his left hand to hold the conducting staff.','This proud musician almost died, and it took him a very long time to get well.','Lully became very sick and passed away in March of that year.'],[],len(PS)-1),
]
